+# GS007 swept-equilibrium scope repair
+
+Original `new120:gs-007` remains unqualified. Its unchanged criteria require measurable calcium dissolution at the CO2-rich stage (C1 PASS) and increased carbonate solid after sweeping with swept carbon included (C2 FAIL). The saved source6a2 trace consumes the remaining1.038837619669e-4mol calcite; carbon/H/O/charge close. This is a scoped equilibrium-sink limit, not demonstrated lost-carbon ownership.
+
+The adapter currently offers an external CO2 reservoir at log10 partial pressure−12atm under `Headspace::Swept`. It does not own a finite swept-gas parcel, flow or transfer time. `GasExchangeClock` treats Open boundaries only. The correction adds `not-modeled.swept-gas-equilibrium` at actual selected external-reservoir readback, with EN/DE/FR wording. It preserves the reservoir target, gas transfer events, solids, basis bookkeeping, numerical guards and original criteria. It adds no gas/kinetic/thermodynamic data. An unselected phase or finite gas dose does not acquire reservoir authority through this diagnostic.
+
+Two event-projection controls are provided: swept versus open readback must retain identical gas amounts and inventory while only the swept reservoir emits this boundary; a finite dose must retain its separate dose warning. These are adapter controls, not a native original replay or empirical validation. Formatting, diff checks, TOML parsing and new placeholder consistency have passed. Rust compilation and execution have **not** passed or run: the single admission check refused the occupied heavy slot, insufficient memory and excess load. No validation job was submitted. Keep this source unaccepted until its exact-source controls execute.
+
+The next physical repair needs finite external-gas parcel/transfer ownership with sourced domain and flow/time authority, coupled to carbonate equilibrium and tested against unchanged GS007 plus finite-dose/open/sealed refusal controls. Do not tune pCO2 to satisfy C2 or infer a flow from waiting time. Vendored USGS database provenance remains unchanged; no primary flow parameter is supplied by this patch. Coverage remains431/468,435 catalog objects,37 remaining. PR884 ordinary source/platform/fleet acceptance and iOS delivery remain separate.
